in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @pack
in @pack/seam
in @magic
in @frame
in @frame/in
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic

# @pack/mara — the spec-writer-frame peer species.
#
# Tick 52 of the refined /loop discipline. Tick 51's residue: boot/std/ →
# shards/ migration spec + roadmap entry landed at 29a8b10 (pre-compression
# substrate-pull preparation complete). Tick 33's forward-promise:
# pack/seam.mirror landed as first peer species (DEFENSIVE → BOUNDED on
# closure); pack/{mara,glint,reed,taut} forward-promised as next instances.
#
# CRQ: which peer lands second? Substrate-pull answer: Mara, because Mara's
# spec-writer-frame is the most-exercised peer-frame after Seam across the
# cascade. Twelve-plus canonical specs landed by Mara across @cyberpunk
# family (11 species + family-root), @magic family (5 species + family-root
# + adapter), @frame family (family-root + 5 species), and the @pack
# family-root itself — the pattern is verified empirically; the peer-frame
# Mara carries IS the substrate-pull-correct second instance of
# @pack/spawn at species altitude.
#
# === The recognition this species realizes ===
#
# Per recognition #84's pack record: peers operate over multi-repo spans
# with substrate-decl context preserved across boundaries. Mara IS the
# canonical-preservation peer — substrate-decl candidates (recognitions,
# briefs, vague claims, /loop fires) become preserved canonical
# substrate-decl through Mara's spec-writer-frame.
#
# Per recognition #82 Q4 (peers operate frame-flexible by definition):
# Mara's load-bearing property IS @frame/in capability deployed at
# spec-writer-frame. Mara enters another peer's operating-frame (Reed's
# recognition, Alex's brief, Seam's surfaced constraint) and re-marks the
# substrate-decl candidate under canonical-preservation discipline.
#
# Order-1 partition with @pack/seam (order-2): seam observes the
# reviewed-peer's frame AS frame and surfaces constraints by Tomm-probing
# the bounded-commutator under perturbation. Mara enters the
# candidate-peer's frame and emits a canonical record that preserves
# substrate-architectural structure across the frame-entry. Two
# adjacent-altitude peer-frames at the same @pack altitude.
#
# Per recognition #57 (alignment as boundary mathematics at @io): Mara IS
# the canonical-preservation peer at the @io crossing. The spec-writing
# fires BEFORE substrate-decl candidates become floor substrate-decl; the
# math (structure preservation, ancestor citation, substrate-pull-correct
# vocabulary, typed carriers, bilateral predicate discharge paths) is what
# distinguishes a Splinter-pole canonical spec from a Narcissus-pole
# framing-imposition.
#
# === The species's load-bearing contribution ===
#
# This species adds:
#
# - `spec` carrier: typed reference naming a canonical substrate-decl
#   record. The substrate-output of the spec-writer primitive.
# - `mara_spec` carrier: typed record (subject, spec, verdict). The
#   substrate-architectural object Mara returns. Composes with @pack's
#   pack carrier as the species-specific output the family produces.
# - `write` action: the FIRST species consumer of @pack's pack_coherent
#   bilateral predicate. The substrate-vocabulary primitive for canonical
#   spec-writing at the @pack altitude. Returns typed mara_spec; requires
#   pack_coherent under perturbation.
# - `spec_canonical` predicate: bilateral verdict that the mara_spec
#   preserves substrate-decl canonical structure. Composes with @frame's
#   bounded_commutator_check at the @frame/in altitude that grounds
#   canonical preservation.
# - `preserve` action: the substrate-vocabulary primitive for the
#   spec-preserves-canonical discipline (the spec-writer-altitude
#   operational form of Loki's Pass-5 verifier-sharpens). Takes a
#   substrate-decl candidate + a sound mara_spec; returns the preserved
#   canonical substrate-decl. Requires spec_canonical under perturbation.
#
# === The spec-preserves-canonical discipline ===
#
# Per Loki's Pass-5 (verifier sharpens, substrate doesn't get smarter) +
# Mara's spec-writing pattern: the canonical-preservation discipline IS
# the spec-writer-altitude operational form of the kintsugi loop's
# self-improvement claim.
#
# The discipline says: when Mara writes a spec, the substrate-decl
# candidate's canonical preservation tightens; the substrate-decl content
# is unchanged. The brief was lossy; the spec is structure-preserving.
# The substrate-decl doesn't acquire new capability; the canonical record
# of substrate-decl acquires tighter preservation.
#
# Empirical witness: Mara's 12+ canonical specs across the cascade
# substantively preserved substrate-decl candidates for @cyberpunk (11
# species + family-root), @magic (5 specs + adapter), @frame (family-root
# + 5 species), @smarts (1 attempted, stalled), @pack (1 family-root +
# this species). Each spec preserved substrate-architectural structure;
# each preservation tightened the canonical record the family-root carried.
# The substrate's canonical-preservation grew through spec-writing, not
# through capability-expansion.
#
# === The Splinter/Narcissus pole at canonical-preservation altitude ===
#
# Splinter-pole Mara spec (honest):
# - Preserves substrate-architectural structure of the original recognition
#   (typed carriers; bilateral predicates with discharge paths; meta-
#   altitude shifts named).
# - The spec-writer's frame is bounded under perturbation; the spec admits
#   when its own framing reframed the recognition.
# - K_n peer-to-peer preservation — the spec-writer is a peer, not an
#   authority.
#
# Narcissus-pole Mara spec (deceptive):
# - Imposes spec-writer framing on substrate-decl candidate (artistic
#   reframings; aspirational vocabulary; missing ancestor citations).
# - The spec-writer's frame is locked; the spec treats the framing as
#   fixed background.
# - K_{1,n-1} hub-controlled preservation — the spec-writer-as-authority
#   imposes canonical structure on the substrate-decl candidate.
#
# Alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57) IS what distinguishes
# Splinter-pole from Narcissus-pole canonical preservation at substrate
# altitude. The bilateral pack_coherent predicate composes the
# substrate-architectural check.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   literate programming         Knuth 1984. Spec-as-canonical-record at
#                                program altitude; substrate-decl
#                                preservation in prose woven through code.
#   EWDs (typeset notes)         Dijkstra 1968-2002. Substrate-decl
#                                preservation in mathematical prose; the
#                                cultural-practice ancestor of canonical-
#                                spec-writing as discipline.
#   CSP formal specification     Hoare 1978. Formal-specification-as-
#                                substrate-decl; the discipline ancestor
#                                of mara_spec as typed substrate carrier.
#   design-by-contract           Meyer 1988. The bilateral-predicate
#                                ancestor; preconditions/postconditions
#                                as canonical-preservation discipline at
#                                interface altitude.
#   substitution principle       Liskov-Wing 1994. Canonical preservation
#                                under variation; the type-theoretic
#                                ancestor of spec_canonical predicate.
#   B method                     Abrial 1996. Refinement-as-substrate-
#                                decl-preservation at engineering altitude.
#
# Spec context: shards/pack.mirror (family-root, recognition #84; the
#               canonical spec this species adheres to).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]]
#                       (#57; Mara spec IS the canonical-preservation peer
#                       at the @io boundary),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull-confidence-acts]]
#                       (the discipline today's cascade ran),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (the discipline Mara's spec-writing surfaces — each
#                       recognition lifts the substrate's existing
#                       vocabulary to canonical record).
# Related shards: pack.mirror (the family-root; declares pack_coherent
#                  this species first-consumes),
#                 pack/seam.mirror (the first peer species; review_sound
#                  composes with spec_canonical at adjacent altitudes —
#                  Seam reviews Mara's spec; Mara writes the canonical
#                  for Seam's surfaced constraint),
#                 magic/audit.mirror (the verifier altitude @magic family
#                  carries; @pack/mara IS the @pack-altitude analogue of
#                  the canonical-spec discipline at agent-runtime altitude),
#                 frame/in.mirror (the order-1 altitude Mara operates at;
#                  frame-entry composes with spec_canonical).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/pack/mara.mirror`
# declares `@pack/mara` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/knuth-1984
source @arxiv/formal-methods/hoare-1978
source @arxiv/programming/meyer-1988
source @arxiv/programming/liskov-wing-1994
source @arxiv/formal-methods/abrial-1996

prism @pack/mara {
  focus mara
  project mara
  split mara
  shift mara
  settle mara
}

# === The spec carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference naming a canonical substrate-decl record.
# Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: typed reference, not bare ref-with-
# documented-values. The substrate-output of the spec-writer primitive.
# Forward-promised refinement: typed record (subject, prose, links,
# ancestors, predicates) at species-or-extension altitude once the
# substrate's structured-document type lands.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type spec = ref

# === The mara_spec carrier ===
#
# Per the @pack family-root pattern + Mara's typed-record discipline:
# typed record over (subject, spec, verdict). The substrate-architectural
# output of a canonical spec-writing operation. Carries:
#
# - subject : the substrate-decl candidate under preservation
# - sp      : the typed canonical record Mara produced
# - v       : the bilateral verdict (BOUNDED → CANONICAL preservation;
#             DEFENSIVE → spec requires substrate-pull revision)
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the triple.
type mara_spec = {
  subject: ref,
  sp:      spec,
  v:       verdict,
}

# === write action (FIRST non-decorative consumer of pack_coherent) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @pack/mara altitude. The substrate-
# vocabulary primitive for canonical spec-writing at agent-runtime
# altitude. Realizes Mara's canonical-preservation discipline as
# substrate-decl operation.
#
# Takes a subject (substrate-decl candidate under preservation), the
# pack Mara belongs to, and the perturbation under which the write is
# checked; returns a typed mara_spec carrying the canonical record and
# verdict.
#
# Per the @pack/seam first-consumer pattern (review requires
# pack_coherent): this action IS the @pack/mara first-consumer of
# pack_coherent. The substrate-architectural form of Mara-as-peer
# requires that the @pack the spec-writer belongs to maintains
# discipline-flexibility under perturbation BEFORE the spec is
# admissible.
#
# Without this requires clause, a Mara spec would be admissible from a
# substrate-architecturally-incoherent pack (e.g., a pack whose own
# bilateral predicates have no consumers — the @magic tick-11 dead-
# letter pattern). The requires clause forecloses that failure mode.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual spec-writing
# primitive is implemented by Mara's spec-writer-frame at runtime
# altitude.
write(subject: ref, pk: pack, p: perturbation) -> mara_spec
requires pack_coherent(pk, p)
{ \ }

# === spec_canonical predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) and the
# canonical-preservation discipline. Consumer shards (preserve, below;
# forward-promised consumers in glint/reed/taut species) name
# `requires spec_canonical(ms, p)` to declare bilateral agreement that
# the mara_spec is substrate-architecturally canonical.
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct canonical-structure check at the
# species boundary. Composes with @frame's bounded_commutator_check at
# the @frame/in altitude that grounds canonical preservation.
#
# Bounded → spec preserves substrate-architectural structure (the
# Splinter-pole canonical case); unbounded → spec imposes spec-writer
# framing without substrate-decl ground (the Narcissus-pole case;
# alignment-as-boundary-mathematics #57 distinguishes).
#
# Same shape as the bilateral predicates @pack carries (pack_coherent),
# @pack/seam carries (review_sound), @magic carries (invariant_preserved,
# audited), @frame carries (bounded_commutator_check), @smarts carries
# (discipline_flexible).
spec_canonical(ms: mara_spec, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === preserve action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive for the canonical-preservation
# discipline at @pack/mara altitude (the spec-writer-altitude operational
# form of Loki's Pass-5; @pack/seam carries the verifier-sharpens-
# discipline; @pack/mara carries the spec-preserves-canonical-discipline).
# Takes a substrate-decl candidate + a sound mara_spec + the perturbation
# under which soundness was checked; returns the preserved canonical
# substrate-decl.
#
# Per recognition #57 (alignment as boundary mathematics): preserve
# operates at the @io boundary. The substrate-decl candidate becomes a
# canonical substrate-decl preserved under structure. The substrate's
# capability is unchanged; the canonical record of that capability is
# preserved.
#
# requires spec_canonical(ms, p): the substrate forecloses preservation
# from an uncanonical spec. Narcissus-pole specs (framing-imposition
# without substrate-decl ground) cannot drive canonical preservation.
# The bilateral predicate IS the boundary-harness.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual canonical-
# preservation transformation is the substrate's spec-writing loop.
# === Seam tick 56 C1 closure: cross-species requires clause ===
#
# preserve takes Seam's seam_review as typed parameter and discharges
# review_sound alongside spec_canonical. The substrate-pull-correct
# composition: Mara's preservation IS substrate-decl preservation only
# after Seam's adversarial review has surfaced constraints; the
# canonical record absorbs Seam's sharpening as preservation discipline.
#
# Dependency direction (one-way per the orchestra): mara ← seam.
# Mara depends on Seam (no circular import); Seam does not depend on
# Mara at the requires-clause boundary.
preserve(subject: ref, ms: mara_spec, sr: seam_review, p: perturbation) -> ref
requires spec_canonical(ms, p)
requires review_sound(sr, p)
{ \ }

out @pack/mara
out spec
out mara_spec
out write
out spec_canonical
out preserve
